  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on setting up the Express server (`server.ts`) to integrate the `@google/genai` library, specifically using `gemini-3.5-flash`. My priority is body parsing within the server file. I want to make sure I am handling this appropriately within the Express framework before I proceed.\n\n\n**Adjusting File Size Limits**\n\nI\'ve realized the default file size limits in Express will be insufficient, particularly for potentially large image uploads. I\'m increasing the limits for `express.json` and `express.urlencoded` to handle up to 10MB files. This ensures robustness when handling larger image data, especially base64 strings. Next up, I will check the structure of our Express endpoint.\n\n\n**Defining Output Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on formatting options. I\'m considering providing a few choices: \"Raw Transcription\", \"Beautiful Markdown\", and a structured JSON output. My goal is to return both raw text and JSON in the backend response to enable the user\'s export option. I need to design the JSON structure, thinking about `text`, `language`, and `confidence` fields.\n\n\n**Developing Structured Output**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a structured output format, inspired by the \"map of intent\" idea. I\'m exploring an array, `structuredLines`, to represent deconstructed visual elements with sequence numbers. This will show the decomposition of the visual data. Also, I\'m thinking about pre-loading a default image in the React UI, specifically a Tamil page, to provide immediate content matching the initial intent!\n\n\n**Implementing Default Image**\n\nI am now thinking about how to handle the initial state of the application. I think I\'ll pre-load a default \"Sample Document,\" specifically a Tamil page, to provide an immediate example when the app starts. It\'s a robust solution! I\'m planning to read and model the Tamil text from the image, and I\'ll focus on creating a perfect default transcription.\nThe text begins with \"vii\" in the top center and continues with a table of contents that includes lines like \"113. D.D.T. \340\256\265\340\256\277\340\256\267\340\256\256\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\223\340\256\260\340\257\215 \340\256\256\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\257\340\256\276\340\256\225\340\256\244\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\277\340\256\261\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\251 \340\256\252\340\257\206\340\256\276\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\263\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\257\210 \340\256\260\340\256\276\340\256\265\340\256\243\340\256\251\340\256\277\340\256\237\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\250\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\257\201 \340\256\252\340\257\206\340\256\261\340\257\215\340\256\261 \340\256\250\340\256\277\340\256\225\340\256\264\340\257\215\340\256\232\340\257\215\340\256\232\340\256\277 -- 123\".\n\n\n**Expanding Output Formatting**\n\nI\'m now thinking about incorporating more of the content from the \"Sample Document.\" I\'ll need to expand my structured output to accurately represent the table of contents and accompanying text. I will add sections like \"Index,\" with lines such as, \"113. D.D.T. \340\256\265\340\256\277\340\256\267\340\256\256\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\223\340\256\260\340\257\215 \340\256\256\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\257\340\256\276\340\256\225\340\256\244\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\277\340\256\261\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\251 \340\256\252\340\257\206\340\256\276\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\263\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\257\210 \340\256\260\340\256\276\340\256\265\340\256\243\340\256\251\340\256\277\340\256\237\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\250\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\257\201 \340\256\252\340\257\206\340\256\261\340\257\215\340\256\261 \340\256\250\340\256\277\340\256\225\340\256\264\340\257\215\340\256\232\340\257\215\340\256\232\340\256\277 -- 123\", to reflect this new structure.\n\n\n**Adding Index Entries**\n\nI\'m expanding the structured output format with more index entries, including details like \"\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\244 \340\256\252\340\257\213\340\256\262\340\256\277\340\256\232\340\257\215 \340\256\232\340\256\276\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\257\340\256\276\340\256\260\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\257\215 -- 192\", \"148. \340\256\205\340\256\251\340\257\215\340\256\251\340\256\277\340\256\257 \340\256\250\340\256\276\340\256\237\340\257\201\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\256\277\340\256\262\340\257\215 \340\256\270\340\256\256\340\257\215\340\256\270\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\257\215\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \342\200\230\340\256\216\340\256\250\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\260\340\257\213 \340\256\256\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\251\340\257\201\340\256\252\340\256\276\340\256\265\340\256\262\340\257\201\342\200\231 \340\256\244\340\257\215\340\256\257\340\256\276\340\256\225\340\256\260\340\256\276\340\256\234 \340\256\270\340\257\215\340\256\265\340\256\276\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\257\215 -- 199\", \"150. \340\256\223\340\256\260\340\257\215 \340\256\265\340\257\207\340\256\250\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\251\340\256\277\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\256\340\257\202\340\256\262\340\256\256\340\257\215 \340\256\244\340\257\206\340\256\257\340\257\215\340\256\265\340\257\200\340\256\225 \340\256\250\340\256\277\340\256\265\340\256\260\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\277 -- 201\". I am also including \"151. \340\256\250\340\256\256\340\256\244\340\257\201 \340\256\250\340\256\276\340\256\237\340\257\215\340\256\237\340\256\277\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\232\340\257\206\340\256\262\340\257\215\340\256\265\340\256\256\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\252\340\256\243\340\257\215\340\256\237\340\257\210\340\256\257 \340\256\216\340\256\225\340\256\277\340\256\252\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\277\340\256\257\340\256\260\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\256\277\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\244\340\256\276\340\256\257\340\257\215\340\256\250\340\256\276\340\256\237\340\257\201 -- 203\", \"153. \340\256\265\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\250\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\277 \340\256\222\340\256\252\340\257\215\340\256\252\340\257\201\340\256\244\340\256\262\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\256\340\256\251\340\257\201\340\256\250\340\257\200\340\256\244\340\256\277 \340\256\232\340\257\213\340\256\264\340\256\260\340\257\215 -- 205\", and \"155. \340\256\252\340\256\262\340\256\276\340\256\244\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\260 \340\256\256\340\256\244 \340\256\256\340\256\276\340\256\261\340\257\215\340\256\261\340\256\256\340\257\215: \340\256\216\340\256\225\340\256\277\340\256\252\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\257\201, \340\256\252\340\256\262\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\257\207\340\256\260\340\256\277\340\256\257\340\256\276, \340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\265\340\256\276, \340\256\256\340\257\206\340\256\225\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\276 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\206\340\256\260\340\256\256\340\257\215\340\256\252 \340\256\225\340\256\277\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\270\340\257\215\340\256\244\340\256\265\340\256\260\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\256\277\340\256\251\340\257\215 \340\256\262\340\256\277\340\256\231\340\257\215\340\256\225 \340\256\265\340\256\264\340\256\277\340\256\252\340\256\276\340\256\237\340\257\201 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\250\340\256\276\340\256\225\340\257\202\340\256\260\340\257\215 \340\256\244\340\256\260\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\276\340\256\265\340\257\201\340\256\256\340\257\215 \340\256\265\340\257\207\340\256\263\340\256\276\340\256\231\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\251\340\257\215\340\256\251\340\256\277\340\256\257\340\257\201\340\256\256\340\257\215 \342\200\224\342\200\224 \340\256\244\340\257\206\340\256\257\340\257\215\340\256\265\340\256\231\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\256\263\340\256\277\340\256\251\340\257\215\".\n\n\n**Refining Default Text**\n\nI\'m now focusing on incorporating the transcribed Tamil text. I am saving the text block as the default text, and also the corresponding image, as a base64 version, and I am storing it for initial display.\n\n\n**Implementing Gemini OCR**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the `@google/genai` SDK and designing the REST API. I\'m building a `POST /api/extract` endpoint to handle base64 image data and specified mime types. The anticipated response will include extracted text, detected language, confidence levels, structured JSON output, and basic stats. I need to make sure `server.ts` is running and communicating with the Vite.config.ts file.\n\n\n**Constructing Image Data Parsing**\n\nI\'m now writing the `server.ts` file, importing `express`, `path`, and `@google/genai`. I\'m handling the undefined `GEMINI_API_KEY` gracefully. Now I\'m writing the `parseBase64Image` function to handle base64 strings with or without prefixes, which will be sent to the Gemini SDK. The SDK requires a mime-type.\n\n\n**Refining Extraction Prompt**\n\nI\'m now refining the Gemini API prompt for OCR. I want high-fidelity extraction without any summarization or alteration. I will prioritize precise Tamil script transcription and structural alignments, such as lists, headings, and so on. Also, I\'m thinking of asking the model to estimate metadata like the detected language(s) and count of structural elements.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the backend Express server `server.ts` to manage server-side Gemini OCR requests. It will parse image uploads, strip base64 meta headers, call Gemini (using the modern `@google/genai` SDK safely on the server), detect languages, and provide a high-confidence transcription, layout metadata, and structural sections."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 121167823
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
