    thinking: "**Considering Example Updates**\n\nI\'m now focusing on whether we need to update the `.env.example` file. It appears it already includes `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL`, so that\'s compliant. Shifting focus, I\'m now exploring the \"Artistic Flair\" styling and considering the specific colors and aesthetic elements involved.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI elements. Specifically, I\'m defining the aesthetic details of the gray neo-brutalist design, starting with component structure, specifically the header, sidebar, and workspace. The plan is to create custom grids and file upload handlers for the left-side workspace, and generate parsed output on the right. Finally, the status bar will provide real-time information. I\'m also ensuring the correct icon imports from lucide-react.\n\n\n**Defining Left-Side Workspace**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the left side, outlining drag-and-drop file upload, and an interactive \"Source Image Page\" component with a scan-HUD animation. I\'m also planning a \"Preload Tamil Document\" feature, allowing automatic loading and representation of the Tamil page, potentially as an illustration with scanning elements, an editable typography mockup, or even a visually recreated interactive paper card. I\'m thinking of options using image generation for the Tamil layout. I\'m excited by these possibilities! I\'m now checking `App.tsx`!\n\n\n**Designing Dynamic User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating dynamic user interaction, envisioning a dual-path approach. First, dynamic image upload will offer live OCR previewing. Second, a preloaded Tamil page sample will showcase the application\'s capabilities, allowing users to extract content from a high-contrast replica with authentic styling. The visual design will be in the neo-brutalist aesthetic, with appropriate fonts and spacing.\n\n\n"
